  "_comment": "Nameserver suffix -> DNS provider map for dns_provider.py and the web app (issue #31). Kept out of records.json, which stays Thundermail-specific. A suffix matches whole labels at the END of a nameserver hostname ('registrar-servers.com' matches 'dns1.registrar-servers.com' but not 'xregistrar-servers.com'); one '*' inside a label matches any run of letters, digits and hyphens ('awsdns-*.com' matches 'ns-1.awsdns-38.com'). Entries are tried in order and the first match wins. 'key' is what dns_provider.py --quiet prints; 'fixes', when present, is the records.json provider block to show (lint-checked in tests/test_dns_provider.py). 'verified': true means the suffix was seen on a live zone at that provider; the rest come from the prototype or provider docs.",
